This spell was discovered by [[Cherit]] on a scroll in the secret laboratory under [[Klaus' bookshop]]. After [[Dante Vale]] read this scroll, Dante used Stopglue to imprison [[unnamed Suit 027]]'s [[Enforcer]] and [[unnamed Suit 028]]'s [[Bonelasher]]. Shortly after, the spell was used to impede [[Klaus]]' [[Brahe]] and then to secure a bookcase to block the team's escape. {{source|The Bookshop Hunter}}

Inside the [[Hamelin Cathedral]], upon getting swarmed my [[Gremlow]]'s special ability, [[Lok Lambert]], [[Sophie Casterwill]] and [[Den Fears]] decide to leave the cathedral to think of a solution to defeat the Titan. To stop the massive flow of Gremlow copies from breaking open the door, Sophie used Stopglue to seal the entrance. {{Source|Gremlow Infestation!}}

Dante used the spell on [[Grand Façade]]'s feet while fighting [[Wilder]] inside [[Hernán Cortés' vault|Hermán Cortés' vault]]. This allowed [[Caliban]] to strike Grand Façade's unprotected back, sending the Titan back to his amulet. {{Source|The Power of Umbra}} 

Several Stopglue spells were cast by both Sophie and Dante as part of an elaborate trap to neutralize the [[Casterwill Hunters]] guarding the entrance to the [[Phoenix Volcano]]. Den also hid the Stopglue spells with [[Hidesight]] so the trap wouldn't be spotted. Four Casterwill Hunters ended up getting stuck on the glue-like substance. Noticing the Soldiers were freeing themselves from the trap, Den and Sophie used several [[Augerfrost]] spells to harden the glue. {{Source|The Phoenix's Ashes}}

Dante used Stopglue in conjunction with [[Bristlebind]] to immobilize [[Hoffman]] while fighting with him on the [[The Professor's castle|The Professor's Castle]]. {{Source|An Ally from the Organization}}

